Multi-license repository — BeccarIA plugin distribution

Copyright (c) 2026 Michele Loi

This repository (`legal-tech-cowork`) hosts the BeccarIA plugin under a
mixed-license model:

1. **MIT** — original BeccarIA parts authored for this project (recognizable
   by the absence of any other license header).
2. **GNU AGPL-3.0-only** — BeccarIA original code that participates in the
   AGPL legal-AI open-source ecosystem (currently:
   `beccaria/skills/ecosystem-scout/` and `beccaria/skills/pattern-extractor/`).
   See `LICENSE-AGPL` for terms.
3. **Apache-2.0** — files inherited from `anthropics/claude-for-legal`
   (the upstream legal-builder-hub plugin), which carry Anthropic's original
   copyright header. See `LICENSE-ANTHROPIC` for the full Apache 2.0 text and
   `NOTICE` for attribution.

Each source file is the authoritative source of its own license: look at the
SPDX-License-Identifier header (when present) or refer to the per-folder
mapping in `LICENSE-AGPL` and to the absence/presence of an Anthropic header.

---

MIT License — for original parts of this repository (the section below
applies to files NOT covered by AGPL-3.0 or Apache-2.0 above):

The following files (and any other file authored originally for this project
— recognizable by the absence of an Anthropic copyright header at the top
AND not listed under AGPL-3.0 in `LICENSE-AGPL`) are released under the MIT
terms below:

- beccaria/skills/adattamento-italiano/
- beccaria/skills/verifica-fonti/
- beccaria/skills/catalogo/adaptation_prompt.md
- bollettino.json (the schema design and the threshold policy)
- BOLLETTINO_FORMAT.md (the threshold policy section in particular)
- README.md, DISTRIBUZIONE.md, BUILD_NOTES.md (project documentation)

Files inherited from `anthropics/claude-for-legal` (the upstream
legal-builder-hub plugin) carry Anthropic's original copyright header and
remain under the Apache License 2.0. See `LICENSE-ANTHROPIC` for the full
Apache 2.0 text, and `NOTICE` for attribution.

